config HOMING_STEP_TEST
	bool "One full step at 446 PPS instead of the homing procedure"
	help
	  The one switch between homing.elf (the homing procedure H0-H5 of
	  dial-me-spinner docs/firmware.md section 5.4) and homing_step.elf:
	  H0 (wake, energise microstep 0 for 10 ms at run current), then one
	  full step toward the click end at 446 PPS (8 microsteps of 7 PWM
	  periods), then SETTLE, brake and sleep. That is the drive of the
	  dial-me-spinner suite's test_firmware_microstep_pwm, which E3's
	  analog check compares against (Phase 1 plan M10).

config HOMING_NEG_FAST
	bool "Negative control: the 446 PPS phases at REFRESH 0 (3125 PPS)"
	help
	  homing_fast.elf, a negative control of make dms-home (ADR-008
	  Amendment 12), not a firmware: homing.elf with the 446 PPS
	  phases (H2 after its first 4 steps, H3) at REFRESH 0, 3125 PPS,
	  seven times firmware.md section 5.3's loaded-zone maximum. The
	  mechanism device has no pull-out or maximum speed (a stated
	  limit), so scripts/check_dms_home.py must fail it from the step
	  rate it measures on the PWM edges.

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
